1
00:00:01,260 --> 00:00:08,919
Chapter 21 Presentiments are strange things, and so are sympathies,

2
00:00:09,500 --> 00:00:13,021
and so are signs, and the three combined make one

3
00:00:13,023 --> 00:00:16,279
mystery to which humanity has not yet found the key.

4
00:00:17,220 --> 00:00:23,220
I never laughed at presentiments in my life because I have had strange ones of my own.

5
00:00:23,959 --> 00:00:29,959
Sympathies, I believe, exist for instance, between far distant, long-absent,

6
00:00:29,961 --> 00:00:34,660
wholly estranged relatives asserting, notwithstanding their alienation,

7
00:00:35,279 --> 00:00:40,760
the unity of the source to which each traces his origin, whose workings baffle

8
00:00:40,760 --> 00:00:44,531
mortal comprehension, and signs, for what we

9
00:00:44,533 --> 00:00:48,220
know, maybe but the sympathies of nature with man.

10
00:00:49,660 --> 00:00:56,080
When I was a little girl, only six years old, I one night heard Bessie Leven say to

11
00:00:56,080 --> 00:01:01,900
Martha Abbott that she had been dreaming about a little child, and that to dream of

12
00:01:01,900 --> 00:01:07,540
children was a sure sign of trouble, either to oneself or one's kin.

13
00:01:08,639 --> 00:01:13,879
The saying might have worn out of my memory had not a circumstance immediately

14
00:01:13,881 --> 00:01:17,919
followed which served indelibly to fix it there.

15
00:01:19,500 --> 00:01:24,919
The next day, Bessie was sent for home to the deathbed of her little sister.

16
00:01:25,900 --> 00:01:30,139
Of late, I had often recalled this saying and this incident.

17
00:01:30,839 --> 00:01:35,720
For during the past week, scarcely a night had gone over my couch that had not

18
00:01:35,720 --> 00:01:40,860
brought with it a dream of an infant, which I sometimes hushed in my arms,

19
00:01:41,559 --> 00:01:46,699
sometimes dandled on my knee, sometimes watched, playing with daisies on a lawn,

20
00:01:47,300 --> 00:01:50,639
or again, dabbling its hands in running water.

21
00:01:50,641 --> 00:01:56,199
It was a wailing child this night, and a laughing one the next.

22
00:01:56,980 --> 00:02:03,239
Now it nestled close to me, and now it ran from me, but whatever mood the apparition

23
00:02:03,241 --> 00:02:08,559
evinced, whatever aspect it wore, it failed not for seven successive nights

24
00:02:08,561 --> 00:02:12,019
to meet me the moment I entered the land of slumber.

25
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:19,940
I did not like this iteration of one idea, this strange recurrence of one image,

26
00:02:20,639 --> 00:02:25,639
and I grew nervous as bedtime approached and the hour of the vision drew near.

27
00:02:26,779 --> 00:02:30,650
It was from companionship with this baby phantom I had

28
00:02:30,650 --> 00:02:34,519
been roused on that moonlight night when I heard the cry.

29
00:02:35,480 --> 00:02:40,559
And it was on the afternoon of the day following, I was summoned downstairs by a

30
00:02:40,561 --> 00:02:44,279
message that someone wanted me in Mrs. Fairfax's room.

31
00:02:46,360 --> 00:02:51,879
On repairing Thither, I found a man waiting for me, having the appearance of a

32
00:02:51,881 --> 00:02:55,828
gentleman servant, he was dressed in deep mourning, and the

33
00:02:55,828 --> 00:02:59,220
hat he held in his hand was surrounded with a crape band.

34
00:03:00,879 --> 00:03:05,900
I dare say you hardly remember me, miss, he said, rising as I entered.

35
00:03:06,919 --> 00:03:08,139
But my name is Levin.

36
00:03:09,139 --> 00:03:12,493
I lived Coachman with Mrs. Reed when you were at Gateshead,

37
00:03:12,493 --> 00:03:15,620
eight or nine years since, and I live there still.

38
00:03:16,540 --> 00:03:18,500
Oh, Robert, how do you do?

39
00:03:19,279 --> 00:03:20,519
I remember you very well.

40
00:03:21,300 --> 00:03:24,959
You used to give me a ride sometimes on Miss Georgiana's Bay Pony.

41
00:03:26,419 --> 00:03:27,900
And how is Bessie?

42
00:03:28,819 --> 00:03:30,400
You are married to Bessie.

43
00:03:31,019 --> 00:03:34,540
Yes, Miss, my wife is very hearty, thank you.

44
00:03:35,099 --> 00:03:38,699
She brought me another little one about two months since, we have three now,

45
00:03:39,480 --> 00:03:41,739
and both mother and child are thriving.

46
00:03:43,480 --> 00:03:45,839
And are the family well at the house, Robert?

47
00:03:47,080 --> 00:03:51,779
I am sorry I can't give you better news of the miss, they are very badly at present,

48
00:03:52,419 --> 00:03:53,459
in great trouble.

49
00:03:55,099 --> 00:03:59,480
I hope no one is dead, I said, glancing at his black dress.

50
00:04:00,220 --> 00:04:03,741
He too looked down at the cape around his hat and replied,

51
00:04:03,741 --> 00:04:07,879
Mr. John died yesterday was a week at his chambers in London.

52
00:04:08,959 --> 00:04:09,959
Mr. John?

53
00:04:10,419 --> 00:04:13,040
Yes, and how does his mother bear it?

54
00:04:14,080 --> 00:04:16,980
Why, you see, Miss Er, it is not a common mishap.

55
00:04:17,760 --> 00:04:19,580
His life has been very wild.

56
00:04:20,440 --> 00:04:23,114
These last three years, he gave himself up

57
00:04:23,114 --> 00:04:26,540
to strange ways, and his death was shocking.

58
00:04:27,480 --> 00:04:29,900
I heard from Bessie he was not doing well.

59
00:04:30,959 --> 00:04:32,059
Doing well?

60
00:04:33,040 --> 00:04:34,040
He could not do worse.

61
00:04:34,779 --> 00:04:39,919
He ruined his health and his estate amongst the worst men and the worst women.

62
00:04:40,879 --> 00:04:42,879
He got into debt and into jail.

63
00:04:43,660 --> 00:04:47,228
His mother helped him out twice, but as soon as he was

64
00:04:47,228 --> 00:04:50,139
free, he returned to his old companions and habits.

65
00:04:51,080 --> 00:04:52,620
His head was not strong.

66
00:04:53,699 --> 00:04:58,019
The naves he lived amongst fooled him beyond anything I ever heard.

67
00:04:58,800 --> 00:05:01,294
He came down to Gateshead about three weeks

68
00:05:01,294 --> 00:05:04,781
ago and wanted misses to give up all to him.

69
00:05:05,639 --> 00:05:06,660
Mrs. refused.

70
00:05:07,360 --> 00:05:12,540
Her means have long been much reduced by his extravagance, so he went back again,

71
00:05:13,139 --> 00:05:14,940
and the next news was that he was dead.

72
00:05:15,819 --> 00:05:17,239
How he died, God knows.

73
00:05:18,059 --> 00:05:19,319
They say he killed himself.

74
00:05:21,180 --> 00:05:22,180
I was silent.

75
00:05:22,720 --> 00:05:24,160
The tidings were frightful.

76
00:05:25,440 --> 00:05:26,800
Robert Leven resumed.

77
00:05:28,379 --> 00:05:30,980
Mrs. had been out of health herself for some time.

78
00:05:31,800 --> 00:05:36,086
She had got very stout, but was not strong with it, and the

79
00:05:36,086 --> 00:05:40,739
loss of money and fear of poverty were quite breaking her down.

80
00:05:41,489 --> 00:05:46,620
The information about Mr. John's death and the manner of it came too suddenly.

81
00:05:47,480 --> 00:05:48,760
It brought on a stroke.

82
00:05:49,620 --> 00:05:51,959
She was three days without speaking.

83
00:05:52,699 --> 00:05:56,120
But last Tuesday, she seemed rather better.

84
00:05:57,059 --> 00:06:00,186
She appeared as if she wanted to say something

85
00:06:00,188 --> 00:06:03,421
and kept making signs to my wife and mumbling.

86
00:06:04,339 --> 00:06:07,239
It was only yesterday morning, however, that

87
00:06:07,241 --> 00:06:09,980
Bessie understood she was pronouncing your name.

88
00:06:10,500 --> 00:06:12,540
And at last, she made out the words.

89
00:06:13,879 --> 00:06:16,400
Bring Jane, fetch Jane air.

90
00:06:16,980 --> 00:06:18,139
I want to speak to her.

91
00:06:19,180 --> 00:06:24,279
Bessie is not sure whether she is in her right mind, or means anything by the

92
00:06:24,281 --> 00:06:30,900
words, but she told Miss Reed and Miss Georgiana, and advised them to send for you.

93
00:06:31,160 --> 00:06:36,339
The young ladies put it off at first, but their mother grew so restless and

94
00:06:36,341 --> 00:06:42,220
said, Jane, Jane so many times that at last they consented.

95
00:06:43,120 --> 00:06:47,004
I left Gateshead yesterday, and if you can get ready, Miss, I

96
00:06:47,004 --> 00:06:50,379
should like to take you back with me early tomorrow morning.

97
00:06:51,419 --> 00:06:53,839
Yes, Robert, I shall be ready.

98
00:06:54,300 --> 00:06:56,199
It seems to me that I ought to go.

99
00:06:57,680 --> 00:06:59,160
I think so too, Miss.

100
00:06:59,900 --> 00:07:01,959
Bessie said she was sure you would not refuse.

101
00:07:03,260 --> 00:07:06,199
But I suppose you will have to ask leave before you can get off.

102
00:07:07,480 --> 00:07:09,559
Yes, and I will do it now.

103
00:07:11,000 --> 00:07:16,260
And having directed him to the servant's hall, and recommended him to the care of

104
00:07:16,260 --> 00:07:23,139
John's wife and the attentions of John himself, I went in search of Mr.

105
00:07:23,319 --> 00:07:24,319
Rochester.

106
00:07:24,580 --> 00:07:26,620
He was not in any of the lower rooms.

107
00:07:27,360 --> 00:07:30,019
He was not in the yard, the stables or the grounds.

108
00:07:30,980 --> 00:07:33,819
I asked Mrs. Fairfax if she had seen him.

109
00:07:34,300 --> 00:07:37,819
Yes, she believed he was playing billiards with Miss Ingram.

110
00:07:39,180 --> 00:07:42,254
To the billiard room I hastened, the click of

111
00:07:42,254 --> 00:07:45,180
balls and the hum of voices resounded dense.

112
00:07:45,839 --> 00:07:49,616
Mr. Rochester, Miss Ingram, the two Mrs. Eshton

113
00:07:49,616 --> 00:07:53,580
and their admirers were all busy in the game.

114
00:07:53,839 --> 00:07:57,180
It required some courage to disturb so interesting a party.

115
00:07:58,319 --> 00:08:02,057
My errand, however, was one I could not defer, so I

116
00:08:02,059 --> 00:08:05,699
approached the master where he stood at Miss Ingram's side.

117
00:08:06,860 --> 00:08:10,620
She turned as I drew near and looked at me haughtily.

118
00:08:11,519 --> 00:08:16,319
Her eyes seemed to demand, what can the creeping creature want now?

119
00:08:17,239 --> 00:08:22,074
And when I said in a low voice, Mr. Rochester, she

120
00:08:22,074 --> 00:08:25,459
made a movement as if tempted to order me away.

121
00:08:26,660 --> 00:08:28,839
I remember her appearance at the moment.

122
00:08:29,419 --> 00:08:32,080
It was very graceful and very striking.

123
00:08:32,699 --> 00:08:35,633
She wore a morning robe of sky blue crape, a

124
00:08:35,633 --> 00:08:39,641
gauzy as your scarf was twisted in her hair.

125
00:08:39,839 --> 00:08:43,665
She had been all animation with the game, an irritated

126
00:08:43,665 --> 00:08:47,260
pride did not lower the expression of her haughty liniments.

127
00:08:48,680 --> 00:08:50,400
Does that person want you?

128
00:08:51,319 --> 00:08:53,160
She inquired of Mr. Rochester.

129
00:08:54,220 --> 00:08:57,760
And Mr. Rochester turned to see who the person was.

130
00:08:58,699 --> 00:09:03,519
He made a curious grimace, one of his strange and equivocal demonstrations,

131
00:09:04,279 --> 00:09:07,419
threw down his cue and followed me from the room.

132
00:09:08,199 --> 00:09:11,065
Well, Jane, he said, as he rested his back

133
00:09:11,067 --> 00:09:15,300
against the schoolroom door which he had shut.

134
00:09:15,559 --> 00:09:19,720
If you please, sir, I want leave of absence for a week or two.

135
00:09:20,300 --> 00:09:21,900
What to do, where to go?

136
00:09:22,699 --> 00:09:24,860
To see a sick lady who has sent for me.

137
00:09:25,779 --> 00:09:26,879
What sick lady?

138
00:09:27,339 --> 00:09:28,339
Where does she live?

139
00:09:28,919 --> 00:09:31,480
At Gateshead in Shire.

140
00:09:32,599 --> 00:09:33,080
Shire.

141
00:09:33,599 --> 00:09:35,339
That is a hundred miles off.

142
00:09:36,000 --> 00:09:38,559
Who may she be that sends for people to see her that distance?

143
00:09:39,739 --> 00:09:41,279
Her name is Reed, sir.

144
00:09:42,099 --> 00:09:42,660
Mrs. Reed.

145
00:09:42,661 --> 00:09:44,519
Reed of Gateshead.

146
00:09:45,000 --> 00:09:47,160
There was a Reed of Gateshead, a magistrate.

147
00:09:48,300 --> 00:09:49,559
It is his widow, sir.

148
00:09:50,379 --> 00:09:52,000
And what have you to do with her?

149
00:09:52,400 --> 00:09:53,400
How do you know her?

150
00:09:54,480 --> 00:09:56,660
Mr. Reed was my uncle, my mother's brother.

151
00:09:57,739 --> 00:09:58,839
The do you see was?

152
00:09:59,580 --> 00:10:00,779
You never told me that before.

153
00:10:00,819 --> 00:10:02,300
You always said you had no relations.

154
00:10:03,360 --> 00:10:04,639
None that would own me, sir.

155
00:10:05,459 --> 00:10:08,379
Mr. Reed is dead, and his wife cast me off.

156
00:10:10,059 --> 00:10:10,739
Why?

157
00:10:10,741 --> 00:10:15,440
Because I was poor and burdened some, and she disliked me.

158
00:10:16,940 --> 00:10:18,720
But Reed left children.

159
00:10:19,559 --> 00:10:20,559
You must have cousins.

160
00:10:21,959 --> 00:10:27,540
Sir George Lynn was talking of a Reed of Gateshead yesterday, who he said was one

161
00:10:27,540 --> 00:10:32,699
of the various rascals on town, and Ingram was mentioning a Georgiana Reed

162
00:10:32,701 --> 00:10:39,161
of the same place, who was much admired for her beauty, a season or two ago in London.

163
00:10:39,680 --> 00:10:41,699
John Reed is dead too, sir.

164
00:10:42,540 --> 00:10:45,108
He ruined himself and half ruined his family,

165
00:10:45,110 --> 00:10:48,381
and his supposed to have committed suicide.

166
00:10:48,800 --> 00:10:53,720
The news so shocked his mother that it brought on an apoplectic attack.

167
00:10:54,919 --> 00:10:56,620
And what good can you do her?

168
00:10:57,059 --> 00:10:58,059
Nonsense, Jane.

169
00:10:58,760 --> 00:11:01,663
I would never think of running a hundred miles to see an

170
00:11:01,665 --> 00:11:05,500
old lady, who will perhaps be dead before you reach her.

171
00:11:06,080 --> 00:11:08,339
Besides, you say she cast you off.

172
00:11:09,260 --> 00:11:14,360
Yes, sir, but that is long ago, and when her circumstances were very

173
00:11:14,360 --> 00:11:17,800
different, I could not be easy to neglect her wishes now.

174
00:11:18,980 --> 00:11:20,199
How long will you stay?

175
00:11:21,199 --> 00:11:23,080
As shorter time as possible, sir.

176
00:11:24,339 --> 00:11:25,839
Promise me only to stay awake.

177
00:11:26,879 --> 00:11:28,959
I had better not pass my word.

178
00:11:29,440 --> 00:11:31,040
I might be obliged to break it.

179
00:11:32,139 --> 00:11:34,199
At all events, you will come back.

180
00:11:35,099 --> 00:11:39,919
You will not be induced under any pretext to take up a permanent residence with her.

181
00:11:40,839 --> 00:11:44,639
Oh no, I shall certainly return if all be well.

182
00:11:45,720 --> 00:11:47,019
And who goes with you?

183
00:11:48,940 --> 00:11:56,940
You don't travel a hundred Yes, sir.

184
00:11:57,639 --> 00:11:59,580
He has lived ten years in the family.

185
00:12:01,139 --> 00:12:02,959
Mr. Rochester meditated.

186
00:12:04,099 --> 00:12:05,540
When do you wish to go?

187
00:12:06,699 --> 00:12:08,139
Early tomorrow morning, sir.

188
00:12:09,379 --> 00:12:11,300
Well, you must have some money.

189
00:12:11,860 --> 00:12:15,160
You can't travel without money, and I dare say you have not much.

190
00:12:15,860 --> 00:12:17,559
I have given you no salary yet.

191
00:12:18,239 --> 00:12:21,540
How much of you in the world, Jane, he asked, smiling.

192
00:12:22,500 --> 00:12:23,680
I drew out my purse.

193
00:12:24,300 --> 00:12:25,300
Amiga thing it was.

194
00:12:26,400 --> 00:12:27,500
Five shilling, sir.

195
00:12:28,260 --> 00:12:31,315
He took the purse, poured the hoard into his palm,

196
00:12:31,315 --> 00:12:34,779
and chuckled over it as if its scantiness amused him.

197
00:12:35,940 --> 00:12:38,120
Soon he produced his pocketbook.

198
00:12:39,080 --> 00:12:41,239
Here said he, offering me a note.

199
00:12:42,120 --> 00:12:44,839
It was fifty pounds and he owed me but fifteen.

200
00:12:46,080 --> 00:12:47,360
I told him I had no change.

201
00:12:48,440 --> 00:12:49,440
I don't want change.

202
00:12:49,739 --> 00:12:50,260
You know that.

203
00:12:50,660 --> 00:12:51,660
Take your wages.

204
00:12:52,260 --> 00:12:55,300
I declined, accepting more than was my due.

205
00:12:56,260 --> 00:13:00,419
He scowled at first, then, as if recollecting something he said,

206
00:13:00,800 --> 00:13:03,239
right, right, better not give you all now.

207
00:13:03,779 --> 00:13:06,699
You would perhaps stay away three months if you had fifty pounds.

208
00:13:07,260 --> 00:13:07,779
There are ten.

209
00:13:08,199 --> 00:13:09,199
Is it not plenty?

210
00:13:10,160 --> 00:13:11,160
Yes, sir.

211
00:13:11,580 --> 00:13:13,160
But now you owe me five.

212
00:13:14,260 --> 00:13:15,260
Come back for it, then.

213
00:13:15,940 --> 00:13:17,620
I am your banker for forty pounds.

214
00:13:18,959 --> 00:13:23,000
Mr. Rochester, I may as well mention another matter

215
00:13:23,002 --> 00:13:25,841
of business to you while I have the opportunity.

216
00:13:26,660 --> 00:13:27,760
Matter of business?

217
00:13:28,660 --> 00:13:30,099
I'm curious to hear it.

218
00:13:30,739 --> 00:13:36,341
You have as good as informed me, sir, that you are going shortly to be married.

219
00:13:36,739 --> 00:13:38,480
Yes, what then?

220
00:13:39,500 --> 00:13:43,180
In that case, sir, a del ought to go to school.

221
00:13:43,959 --> 00:13:46,800
I am sure you will perceive the necessity of it.

222
00:13:48,040 --> 00:13:49,760
To get her out of my bride's way.

223
00:13:50,540 --> 00:13:53,660
Who might otherwise walk over her rather too emphatically?

224
00:13:54,919 --> 00:13:58,000
There's sense in the suggestion, not a doubt of it.

225
00:13:58,599 --> 00:14:01,699
A del, as you say, must go to school.

226
00:14:02,199 --> 00:14:07,300
And you, of course, must march straight to the devil.

227
00:14:08,379 --> 00:14:12,220
I hope not, sir, but I must seek another situation somewhere.

228
00:14:13,660 --> 00:14:18,620
In course, he exclaimed, with a twang of voice and a distortion of features,

229
00:14:19,239 --> 00:14:20,879
equally fantastic and ludicrous.

230
00:14:21,860 --> 00:14:23,139
He looked at me some minutes.

231
00:14:24,599 --> 00:14:28,086
An old madam read, or the misses, her daughters,

232
00:14:28,088 --> 00:14:30,839
will be solicited by you to seek a place, I suppose?

233
00:14:32,360 --> 00:14:33,360
No, sir.

234
00:14:33,980 --> 00:14:36,964
I am not on such terms with my relatives as would justify

235
00:14:36,966 --> 00:14:40,459
me in asking favors of them, but I shall advertise.

236
00:14:41,980 --> 00:14:45,900
You shall walk up the pyramids of Egypt, he growled.

237
00:14:47,019 --> 00:14:48,839
At your peril, you advertise.

238
00:14:50,120 --> 00:14:53,199
I wish I had only offered you a sovereign instead of ten pounds.

239
00:14:54,360 --> 00:14:57,440
Give me back nine pounds, Jane, I have a use for it.

240
00:14:58,860 --> 00:15:03,699
And so have I, sir, I returned, putting my hands and my purse behind me.

241
00:15:04,739 --> 00:15:07,099
I could not spare the money on any account.

242
00:15:08,080 --> 00:15:14,879
Little niggard said he, refusing me a pecuniary request, give me five pounds, Jane.

243
00:15:15,220 --> 00:15:17,260
Not five shilling, sir, nor five pence.

244
00:15:18,199 --> 00:15:19,360
Just let me look at the cash.

245
00:15:20,260 --> 00:15:22,480
No, sir, you are not to be trusted.

246
00:15:23,660 --> 00:15:27,620
Jane, sir, promise me one thing.

247
00:15:29,040 --> 00:15:32,720
I'll promise you anything, sir, that I think I am likely to perform.

248
00:15:33,879 --> 00:15:35,957
Not to advertise and to trust this quest of

249
00:15:35,959 --> 00:15:39,421
a situation to me, I'll find you one in time.

250
00:15:39,739 --> 00:15:44,559
I shall be glad so to do, sir, if you in your turn will promise that I

251
00:15:44,561 --> 00:15:48,879
and Adele shall be both safe out of the house before your bride enters it.

252
00:15:50,059 --> 00:15:54,199
Very well, very well, I'll pledge my word on it.

253
00:15:54,940 --> 00:15:55,940
You go tomorrow then?

254
00:15:56,760 --> 00:15:58,199
Yes, sir, early.

255
00:15:59,319 --> 00:16:01,739
Shall you come down to the drawing room after dinner?

256
00:16:03,040 --> 00:16:05,660
No, sir, I must prepare for the journey.

257
00:16:06,760 --> 00:16:09,540
Then you and I must bid goodbye for a little while.

258
00:16:10,339 --> 00:16:11,500
I suppose so, sir.

259
00:16:12,540 --> 00:16:15,699
And how do people perform that ceremony of parting, Jane?

260
00:16:16,839 --> 00:16:17,839
Teach me.

261
00:16:17,940 --> 00:16:18,940
I'm not quite up to it.

262
00:16:19,940 --> 00:16:23,260
They say farewell or any other form they prefer.

263
00:16:23,879 --> 00:16:24,959
Then say it.

264
00:16:25,919 --> 00:16:27,959
Farewell, Mr. Rochester, for the present.

265
00:16:29,000 --> 00:16:30,000
What must I say?

266
00:16:30,940 --> 00:16:32,339
The same, if you like, sir.

267
00:16:33,279 --> 00:16:34,720
Farewell, miss air, for the present.

268
00:16:35,440 --> 00:16:36,440
Is that all?

269
00:16:37,279 --> 00:16:38,279
Yes.

270
00:16:38,860 --> 00:16:43,559
It seems stingy to my notions and dry and unfriendly.

271
00:16:44,519 --> 00:16:48,220
I should like something else, a little addition to the right.

272
00:16:49,040 --> 00:16:53,300
If one shook hands, for instance, but no, that would not content me either.

273
00:16:54,279 --> 00:16:56,660
So you'll do no more than say farewell, Jane.

274
00:16:57,760 --> 00:17:03,099
It is enough, sir, as much good will may be conveyed in one hearty word as in many.

275
00:17:04,199 --> 00:17:07,379
Very likely, but it is blank and cool.

276
00:17:09,019 --> 00:17:10,019
Farewell.

277
00:17:10,739 --> 00:17:14,400
How long is he going to stand with his back against that door?

278
00:17:15,059 --> 00:17:16,059
I ask myself.

279
00:17:16,739 --> 00:17:18,260
I want to commence my packing.

280
00:17:19,260 --> 00:17:24,160
The dinner-bell rang, and suddenly away he bolted, without another syllable.

281
00:17:25,040 --> 00:17:30,061
I saw him no more during the day, and was off before he had risen in the morning.

282
00:17:30,379 --> 00:17:32,720
I reached the lodge at Gateshead about five

283
00:17:32,720 --> 00:17:36,161
o'clock in the afternoon of the first of May.

284
00:17:36,559 --> 00:17:38,860
I stepped in there before going up to the hall.

285
00:17:39,559 --> 00:17:41,319
It was very clean and neat.

286
00:17:42,199 --> 00:17:45,120
The ornamental windows were hung with little white curtains.

287
00:17:46,000 --> 00:17:47,220
The floor was spotless.

288
00:17:48,000 --> 00:17:52,139
The great and fire ions were burnished bright, and the fire burnt clear.

289
00:17:53,620 --> 00:17:59,019
Bessie sat on the hearth, nursing her last born, and Robert and his sister,

290
00:17:59,620 --> 00:18:01,360
played quietly in a corner.

291
00:18:02,680 --> 00:18:03,680
Bless you.

292
00:18:03,879 --> 00:18:06,980
I knew you would come, exclaimed Mrs. Levin, as I entered.

293
00:18:08,239 --> 00:18:12,540
Yes, Bessie, said I, after I had kissed her, and I trust I am not too late.

294
00:18:13,480 --> 00:18:14,480
How is Mrs. Reed?

295
00:18:15,139 --> 00:18:16,360
Alive, still, I hope?

296
00:18:17,040 --> 00:18:22,339
Yes, she is alive, and more sensible and collected than she was.

297
00:18:23,319 --> 00:18:26,262
The doctor says she may linger a week or two yet,

298
00:18:26,264 --> 00:18:29,260
but he hardly thinks she will finally recover.

299
00:18:31,360 --> 00:18:32,480
Has she mentioned me lately?

300
00:18:33,940 --> 00:18:40,220
She was talking of you only this morning and wishing you would come, but she is

301
00:18:40,220 --> 00:18:45,019
sleeping now, or was ten minutes ago when I was up at the house.

302
00:18:46,080 --> 00:18:49,288
She generally lies in a kind of lethargy all

303
00:18:49,290 --> 00:18:53,120
the afternoon and wakes up about six or seven.

304
00:18:53,980 --> 00:18:55,940
Will you rest yourself here an hour, Miss?

305
00:18:56,959 --> 00:18:58,580
And then I will go up with you.

306
00:18:59,459 --> 00:19:03,036
Robert here entered, and Bessie laid her sleeping

307
00:19:03,036 --> 00:19:06,360
child in the cradle and went to welcome him.

308
00:19:06,660 --> 00:19:11,459
Afterwards, she insisted on my taking off my bonnet and having some tea.

309
00:19:12,480 --> 00:19:14,839
For she said I looked pale and tired.

310
00:19:15,900 --> 00:19:21,040
I was glad to accept her hospitality, and I submitted to be relieved of my

311
00:19:21,040 --> 00:19:26,819
traveling garb just as passively as I used to let her undress me when a child.

312
00:19:28,419 --> 00:19:34,400
Old times crowded fast back on me as I watched her bustling about, setting out

313
00:19:34,400 --> 00:19:39,120
the tea tray with her best china, cutting bread and butter, toasting a tea

314
00:19:39,120 --> 00:19:46,339
cake, and between wiles giving little Robert or Jane an occasional tap or push

315
00:19:46,341 --> 00:19:49,699
just as she used to give me in former days.

316
00:19:52,080 --> 00:19:55,980
Bessie had retained her quick temper as well as her light foot and good looks.

317
00:19:57,019 --> 00:20:01,779
Tea-ready, I was going to approach the table, but she desired me to sit still,

318
00:20:02,360 --> 00:20:04,400
quite in her old peremptory tones.

319
00:20:05,440 --> 00:20:08,500
I must be served at the fireside, she said.

320
00:20:09,440 --> 00:20:14,220
And she placed before me a little round stand with my cup and a plate of toast,

321
00:20:15,260 --> 00:20:18,313
absolutely as she used to accommodate me with some

322
00:20:18,315 --> 00:20:21,281
privately perloined dainty on a nursery chair.

323
00:20:21,839 --> 00:20:25,160
And I smiled and obeyed her as in by gone days.

324
00:20:26,480 --> 00:20:31,879
She wanted to know if I was happy at Thornfield Hall, and what sort of a person

325
00:20:31,881 --> 00:20:35,815
the mistress was, and when I told her there was only a

326
00:20:35,817 --> 00:20:39,260
master, whether he was a nice gentleman and if I liked him.

327
00:20:40,500 --> 00:20:44,029
I told her he was rather an ugly man, but quite a

328
00:20:44,031 --> 00:20:48,199
gentleman, and that he treated me kindly and I was content.

329
00:20:49,260 --> 00:20:52,326
Then I went on to describe to her the gay company

330
00:20:52,328 --> 00:20:55,461
that had lately been staying at the house.

331
00:20:55,779 --> 00:20:59,120
And to these details, Bessie listened with interest.

332
00:21:00,000 --> 00:21:02,699
They were precisely of the kind she relished.

333
00:21:04,019 --> 00:21:06,959
In such conversation, an hour was soon gone.

334
00:21:07,959 --> 00:21:10,000
Bessie restored to me my bonnet, etc.

335
00:21:10,779 --> 00:21:14,180
And, accompanied by her, I quit at the lodge for the hall.

336
00:21:14,919 --> 00:21:19,004
It was also accompanied by her that I had, nearly nine

337
00:21:19,006 --> 00:21:22,339
years ago, walked down the path I was now ascending.

338
00:21:22,940 --> 00:21:30,940
On a dark, misty, raw morning in January, I had left a hostile roof with a desperate

339
00:21:30,940 --> 00:21:37,400
and embittered heart, a sense of outlawry and almost of reprobation, to seek the

340
00:21:37,400 --> 00:21:41,779
chilly harbourage of lowered, that bore so far away and unexplored.

341
00:21:42,540 --> 00:21:46,220
The same hostile roof now again rose before me.

342
00:21:46,839 --> 00:21:50,980
My prospects were doubtful yet, and I had yet an aching heart.

343
00:21:52,279 --> 00:21:57,319
I still felt as a wanderer on the face of the earth, but I experienced firm a trust

344
00:21:57,321 --> 00:22:01,940
in myself and my own powers, and less withering dread of oppression.

345
00:22:03,220 --> 00:22:06,372
The gaping wound of my wrongs too was now quite

346
00:22:06,374 --> 00:22:10,699
healed, and the flame of resentment extinguished.

347
00:22:11,940 --> 00:22:15,644
You shall go into the breakfast room first, said

348
00:22:15,644 --> 00:22:18,540
Bessie, as she preceded me through the hall.

349
00:22:19,180 --> 00:22:20,879
The young ladies will be there.

350
00:22:22,059 --> 00:22:25,099
In another moment, I was within that apartment.

351
00:22:26,160 --> 00:22:29,580
There was every article of furniture looking just as it did,

352
00:22:29,582 --> 00:22:33,919
on the morning I was first introduced to Mr. Brocklehurst.

353
00:22:34,519 --> 00:22:38,760
The very rug he had stood upon still covered the hearth.

354
00:22:39,599 --> 00:22:44,220
Glancing at the bookcases, I thought I could distinguish the two volumes of

355
00:22:44,220 --> 00:22:49,860
Bewick's British birds, occupying their old place on the third shelf, and

356
00:22:49,860 --> 00:22:54,160
Gulliver's travels and the Arabian knights ranged just above.

357
00:22:55,599 --> 00:22:59,281
The inanimate objects were not changed, but the

358
00:22:59,283 --> 00:23:02,699
living things had altered, passed recognition.

359
00:23:03,699 --> 00:23:09,000
Two young ladies appeared before me, one very tall, almost as tall as Miss

360
00:23:09,000 --> 00:23:13,639
Ingram, very thin too, with a shallow face and severe mean.

361
00:23:14,839 --> 00:23:19,819
There was something aesthetic in her look, which was augmented by the extreme

362
00:23:19,821 --> 00:23:25,839
planeness of a straight skirted, black stuffed dress, a starched linen

363
00:23:25,841 --> 00:23:30,296
collar, hair combed away from the temples, and the none-like

364
00:23:30,298 --> 00:23:34,519
ornament of a string of ebony beads and a crucifix.

365
00:23:35,319 --> 00:23:40,760
This I felt sure was Eliza, though I could trace little resemblance to her former

366
00:23:40,760 --> 00:23:44,879
self in that elongated and colourless visage.

367
00:23:45,980 --> 00:23:49,855
The other was as certainly Georgiana, but not the Georgiana

368
00:23:49,857 --> 00:23:54,160
I remembered, the slim and fairy-like girl of eleven.

369
00:23:55,220 --> 00:24:01,839
This was a full-blown, very plump damsel, fair as wax work, with handsome and

370
00:24:01,841 --> 00:24:07,139
regular features, languishing blue eyes, and ringleted yellow hair.

371
00:24:08,040 --> 00:24:12,980
The hue of her dress was black too, but its fashion was so different from her

372
00:24:12,980 --> 00:24:16,677
sisters, so much more flowing and becoming, it

373
00:24:16,678 --> 00:24:20,040
looked as stylish as the others looked puritanical.

374
00:24:21,260 --> 00:24:26,040
In each of the sisters there was one trait of the mother, and only one.

375
00:24:26,860 --> 00:24:31,500
The thin and pallid elder daughter had her parents' care and gorm eye.

376
00:24:32,680 --> 00:24:37,620
The blooming and luxuriant younger girl had her contour of jaw and chin.

377
00:24:38,500 --> 00:24:46,099
Perhaps a little softened, but still imparting an indescribable hardness to the

378
00:24:46,101 --> 00:24:50,319
countenance otherwise, so voluptuous and boxum.

379
00:24:51,839 --> 00:24:55,417
Both ladies, as I advanced, rose to welcome me

380
00:24:55,419 --> 00:24:58,980
and both addressed me by the name of Miss Air.

381
00:25:00,180 --> 00:25:06,800
Eliza's greeting was delivered in a short abrupt voice without a smile, and then she

382
00:25:06,800 --> 00:25:11,779
sat down again, fixed her eyes on the fire and seemed to forget me.

383
00:25:12,639 --> 00:25:15,260
Georgiana added to her, how do you do?

384
00:25:16,160 --> 00:25:21,260
Several common places about my journey, the weather, and so on, uttered in rather

385
00:25:21,260 --> 00:25:24,512
a drawing tone, and accompanied by sundry side

386
00:25:24,512 --> 00:25:28,561
glances that measured me from head to foot.

387
00:25:28,860 --> 00:25:33,124
Now traversing the folds of my drab marino police, and

388
00:25:33,125 --> 00:25:37,300
now lingering on the plain trimming of my cottage bonnet.

389
00:25:38,400 --> 00:25:42,273
Young ladies have a remarkable way of letting you know that

390
00:25:42,275 --> 00:25:46,000
they think you acquies without actually saying the words.

391
00:25:47,339 --> 00:25:52,879
A certain superciliousness of look, coolness of manner, nonchalance of tone,

392
00:25:53,559 --> 00:25:56,832
express fully their sentiments on the point, without

393
00:25:56,832 --> 00:26:00,739
committing them by any positive rudeness in word or deed.

394
00:26:01,779 --> 00:26:06,180
A sneer, however, whether covert or open, had now

395
00:26:06,182 --> 00:26:09,800
no longer that power over me it once possessed.

396
00:26:10,559 --> 00:26:15,940
As I sat between my cousins, I was surprised to find how easy I felt under

397
00:26:15,940 --> 00:26:20,300
the total neglect of the one and the semi -sarcastic attentions of the other.

398
00:26:21,139 --> 00:26:24,400
Eliza did not modify nor Georgiana ruffle me.

399
00:26:25,040 --> 00:26:28,139
The fact was I had other things to think about.

400
00:26:28,919 --> 00:26:32,385
Within the last few months feelings had been stirred

401
00:26:32,387 --> 00:26:36,400
in me so much more potent than any they could raise.

402
00:26:37,260 --> 00:26:42,959
Pains and pleasures so much more acute and exquisite had been excited than any.

403
00:26:43,660 --> 00:26:47,122
It was in their power to inflict or bestow that

404
00:26:47,122 --> 00:26:51,099
their ears gave me no concern either for good or bad.

405
00:26:52,680 --> 00:26:53,959
How is Mrs. Reed?

406
00:26:54,819 --> 00:27:00,220
I asked soon, looking calmly at Georgiana, who thought fit to bridle at the direct

407
00:27:00,220 --> 00:27:03,419
address, as if it were an unexpected liberty.

408
00:27:04,819 --> 00:27:05,819
Mrs. Reed?

409
00:27:06,440 --> 00:27:10,000
Ah, ma'am, you mean she is extremely poorly.

410
00:27:10,519 --> 00:27:11,919
I doubt if you can see her tonight.

411
00:27:12,559 --> 00:27:16,254
If, said I, you would just step upstairs and tell

412
00:27:16,256 --> 00:27:19,461
her I'm come, I should be much obliged to you.

413
00:27:20,260 --> 00:27:25,480
Georgiana almost started and she opened her blue eyes wild and wide.

414
00:27:26,680 --> 00:27:31,639
I know she had a particular wish to see me, I added, and I would not defer

415
00:27:31,641 --> 00:27:35,500
attending to her desire longer than is absolutely necessary.

416
00:27:36,339 --> 00:27:40,959
Mama dislikes being disturbed in an evening, remarked Eliza.

417
00:27:41,779 --> 00:27:48,699
I soon rose, quietly took off my bonnet and gloves, uninvited, and said I would

418
00:27:48,701 --> 00:27:54,260
just step out to Bessie, who was, I dared say, in the kitchen, and asked her

419
00:27:54,260 --> 00:27:59,040
to ascertain whether Mrs. Reed was disposed to receive me or not tonight.

420
00:27:59,860 --> 00:28:04,118
I went, and having found Bessie and dispatched her

421
00:28:04,118 --> 00:28:07,080
on my errand, I proceeded to take further measures.

422
00:28:07,980 --> 00:28:12,279
It adhered to forebeen my habit, always to shrink from arrogance.

423
00:28:14,459 --> 00:28:18,218
Received as I had been today, I should a year ago

424
00:28:18,218 --> 00:28:21,620
have resolved to quit Gateshead the very next morning.

425
00:28:22,540 --> 00:28:27,819
Now, it was disclosed to me all at once that that would be a foolish plan.

426
00:28:28,760 --> 00:28:32,292
I had taken a journey of a hundred miles to see my aunt,

427
00:28:32,292 --> 00:28:36,680
and I must stay with her till she was better, or dead.

428
00:28:37,879 --> 00:28:43,599
As to her daughter's pride or folly, I must put it on one side, make myself

429
00:28:43,601 --> 00:28:50,319
independent of it, so I addressed the housekeeper, asked her to show me a room,

430
00:28:51,300 --> 00:28:56,000
told her I should probably be a visitor here for a week or two, had my trunk

431
00:28:56,000 --> 00:28:59,459
conveyed to my chamber, and followed it with her myself.

432
00:29:00,339 --> 00:29:02,400
I met Bessie on the landing.

433
00:29:03,760 --> 00:29:07,947
Mrs. Is a wake, said she, I have told her you are

434
00:29:07,947 --> 00:29:11,580
here, come and let us see if she will know you.

435
00:29:12,699 --> 00:29:18,040
I did not need to be guided to the well -known room, to which I had so often been

436
00:29:18,040 --> 00:29:21,500
summoned for chastisement or reprimand in former days.

437
00:29:22,319 --> 00:29:26,220
I hastened before Bessie, I softly opened the door.

438
00:29:27,080 --> 00:29:31,660
A shaded light stood on the table, for it was now getting dark.

439
00:29:32,559 --> 00:29:37,919
There was the great four-post bed with amber hangings as of old, there the toilet

440
00:29:37,921 --> 00:29:43,180
table, the armchair, and the footstool, at which I had a hundred times been

441
00:29:43,180 --> 00:29:47,919
sentenced to kneel, to ask pardon for offenses by me uncommitted.

442
00:29:49,160 --> 00:29:55,239
I looked into a certain corner near, half expecting to see the slim outline of

443
00:29:55,241 --> 00:30:01,559
a once dreaded switch, which used to lurk there, waiting to leap out imp like,

444
00:30:02,160 --> 00:30:04,680
and lace my quivering palm or shrinking neck.

445
00:30:05,980 --> 00:30:07,480
I approached the bed.

446
00:30:08,339 --> 00:30:11,879
I opened the curtains and lent over the high piled pillows.

447
00:30:13,019 --> 00:30:18,841
Well, did I remember Mrs. Reed's face, and I eagerly sought to the familiar image.

448
00:30:19,239 --> 00:30:22,650
It is a happy thing that time quells the longings of

449
00:30:22,652 --> 00:30:25,940
vengeance and hushes the promptings of rage and aversion.

450
00:30:26,980 --> 00:30:31,620
I had left this woman in bitterness and hate, and I came back to her now with no

451
00:30:31,620 --> 00:30:37,000
other emotion than a sort of roof for her great sufferings, and a strong yearning to

452
00:30:37,000 --> 00:30:44,161
forget and forgive all injuries, to be reconciled and classed hands in amity.

453
00:30:44,400 --> 00:30:49,360
The well-known face was there, stern, relentless as ever.

454
00:30:49,980 --> 00:30:53,516
There was that peculiar eye which nothing could melt,

455
00:30:53,516 --> 00:30:57,239
and the somewhat raised imperious despotic eyebrow.

456
00:30:58,199 --> 00:31:03,279
How often had it lowered on me menace and hate, and how the recollection of

457
00:31:03,281 --> 00:31:08,364
childhood's terrors and sorrows revived as I traced its

458
00:31:08,364 --> 00:31:11,720
harsh line now, and yet I stooped down and kissed her.

459
00:31:12,480 --> 00:31:13,480
She looked at me.

460
00:31:14,900 --> 00:31:17,360
Is this Jane Eyre, she said?

461
00:31:18,360 --> 00:31:19,480
Yes, aren't read.

462
00:31:20,180 --> 00:31:21,279
How are you dear Aunt?

463
00:31:22,519 --> 00:31:26,099
I had once vowed that I would never call her Aunt again.

464
00:31:27,199 --> 00:31:30,279
I thought it no sin to forget and break that vow now.

465
00:31:31,559 --> 00:31:35,379
My fingers had fastened on her hand which lay outside the sheet.

466
00:31:36,480 --> 00:31:42,540
Had she pressed mine kindly, I should at that moment have experienced true pleasure.

467
00:31:43,379 --> 00:31:47,254
But unimpressionable natures are not so soon softened,

468
00:31:47,254 --> 00:31:50,900
nor are natural antipathies so readily eradicated.

469
00:31:52,519 --> 00:31:55,898
Mrs. Reed took her hand away, and turning her face

470
00:31:55,898 --> 00:31:59,260
rather from me, she remarked that the night was warm.

471
00:31:59,940 --> 00:32:01,839
Again, she regarded me so isolated.

472
00:32:02,839 --> 00:32:06,561
I felt at once that her opinion of me, her feeling

473
00:32:06,561 --> 00:32:09,741
towards me, was unchanged and unchangeable.

474
00:32:10,220 --> 00:32:16,180
I knew by her stony eye, opaque to tenderness, indisoluble to tears,

475
00:32:17,080 --> 00:32:19,860
that she was resolved to consider me bad to the last.

476
00:32:20,739 --> 00:32:23,705
Because to believe me good, would give her no

477
00:32:23,705 --> 00:32:26,980
generous pleasure, only a sense of mortification.

478
00:32:27,519 --> 00:32:34,599
I felt pain, and then I felt anger, and then I felt a determination to subdue

479
00:32:34,601 --> 00:32:39,059
her, to be her mistress in spite both of her nature and her will.

480
00:32:40,400 --> 00:32:45,500
My tears had risen, just as in childhood, I ordered them back to their source,

481
00:32:46,360 --> 00:32:50,699
I brought a chair to the bedhead, I sat down and leaned over the pillow.

482
00:32:52,319 --> 00:32:56,519
You sent for me, I said, and I am here, and it is

483
00:32:56,519 --> 00:33:00,040
my intention to stay till I see how you get on.

484
00:33:00,660 --> 00:33:01,660
Oh, of course.

485
00:33:02,459 --> 00:33:03,540
You have seen my daughters?

486
00:33:04,400 --> 00:33:05,400
Yes.

487
00:33:05,919 --> 00:33:09,491
Well, you may tell them, I wish you to stay, till I

488
00:33:09,493 --> 00:33:12,559
can talk some things over with you I have on my mind.

489
00:33:13,480 --> 00:33:17,275
Tonight it is too late, and I have a difficulty in recalling

490
00:33:17,277 --> 00:33:20,739
them, but there was something I wish to say, let me see.

491
00:33:22,099 --> 00:33:26,027
The wandering look and changed utterance told what

492
00:33:26,027 --> 00:33:29,599
wreck had taken place in her once vigorous frame.

493
00:33:30,959 --> 00:33:35,000
Turning restlessly, she drew the bedclothes round her, my elbow,

494
00:33:35,639 --> 00:33:39,699
resting on a corner of the quilt, fixed it down, she was at once irritated.

495
00:33:41,220 --> 00:33:46,239
Sit up, said she, don't annoy me with holding the clothes fast.

496
00:33:46,879 --> 00:33:47,879
Are you Jane Eyre?

497
00:33:48,660 --> 00:33:49,900
I am Jane Eyre.

498
00:33:50,540 --> 00:33:54,059
I have had more trouble with that child than anyone would believe.

499
00:33:54,940 --> 00:34:00,559
Such a burden to be left on my hands, and so much annoyance as she caused me,

500
00:34:01,260 --> 00:34:06,440
daily and hourly, with her incomprehensible disposition, and her

501
00:34:06,440 --> 00:34:13,120
sudden starts of temper, and her continual unnatural watchings of one's movements.

502
00:34:14,400 --> 00:34:18,559
I declare she talked to me once like something mad or like a fiend.

503
00:34:19,319 --> 00:34:21,480
No child ever spoke or looked as she did.

504
00:34:22,220 --> 00:34:24,099
I was glad to get her away from the house.

505
00:34:25,379 --> 00:34:27,040
What did they do with her at Lohwood?

506
00:34:27,940 --> 00:34:30,739
The fever broke out there, and many of the pupils died.

507
00:34:31,620 --> 00:34:35,400
She, however, did not die, but I said she did.

508
00:34:36,139 --> 00:34:37,279
I wish she had died.

509
00:34:38,680 --> 00:34:40,279
A strange wish, Mrs. Reed.

510
00:34:40,980 --> 00:34:41,980
Why do you hate her so?

511
00:34:43,160 --> 00:34:47,839
I had a dislike to her mother always, for she was my husband's only sister,

512
00:34:48,599 --> 00:34:50,220
and a great favorite with him.

513
00:34:50,959 --> 00:34:55,279
He opposed the families disowning her when she made her low marriage.

514
00:34:56,339 --> 00:35:00,760
And when news came of her death, he wept like a simpleton.

515
00:35:01,779 --> 00:35:05,648
He would send for the baby, though I entreated him rather

516
00:35:05,650 --> 00:35:08,319
to put it out to nurse and pay for its maintenance.

517
00:35:09,180 --> 00:35:15,160
I hated it the first time I set my eyes on it, a sickly whining, pining thing.

518
00:35:15,919 --> 00:35:19,766
It would wail in its cradle all night long, not screaming

519
00:35:19,766 --> 00:35:23,360
heartily like any other child but whimpering and moaning.

520
00:35:24,540 --> 00:35:30,879
Reed pitted it, and he used to nurse it and notice it as if it had been his own.

521
00:35:31,800 --> 00:35:35,319
More indeed than he ever noticed his own at that age.

522
00:35:36,580 --> 00:35:40,000
He would try to make my children friendly to the little beggar.

523
00:35:40,720 --> 00:35:43,294
The darlings could not bear it, and he was

524
00:35:43,296 --> 00:35:46,199
angry with them when they showed their dislike.

525
00:35:47,480 --> 00:35:53,540
In his last illness, he had it brought continually to his bedside, and but an

526
00:35:53,540 --> 00:35:58,239
hour before he died, he bound me by vow to keep the creature.

527
00:35:59,180 --> 00:36:03,419
I would as soon have been charged with a pauper brat out of a workhouse,

528
00:36:04,120 --> 00:36:06,440
but he was weak, naturally weak.

529
00:36:07,220 --> 00:36:11,440
John does not at all resemble his father, and I am glad of it.

530
00:36:12,139 --> 00:36:14,319
John is like me, and like my brothers.

531
00:36:15,300 --> 00:36:16,580
He is quite a gibson.

532
00:36:17,379 --> 00:36:21,239
Oh, I wish he would cease tormenting me with letters for money.

533
00:36:22,319 --> 00:36:24,239
I have no more money to give him.

534
00:36:24,620 --> 00:36:25,620
We are getting poor.

535
00:36:26,620 --> 00:36:31,459
I must send away half the servants and shut up part of the house, or let it off.

536
00:36:32,400 --> 00:36:35,739
I can never submit to do that, yet how are we to get on?

537
00:36:36,819 --> 00:36:40,599
Two-thirds of my income goes in paying the interest of mortgages.

538
00:36:41,480 --> 00:36:45,559
John gambles dreadfully, and always loses poor boy.

539
00:36:46,160 --> 00:36:47,599
He is beset by sharpers.

540
00:36:48,180 --> 00:36:49,860
John is sunk and degraded.

541
00:36:49,959 --> 00:36:51,540
His look is frightful.

542
00:36:52,500 --> 00:36:54,580
I feel ashamed for him when I see him.

543
00:36:55,699 --> 00:36:57,300
She was getting much excited.

544
00:36:58,500 --> 00:37:01,205
I think I'd better leave her now," said I to

545
00:37:01,205 --> 00:37:04,881
Bessie, who stood on the other side of the bed.

546
00:37:05,580 --> 00:37:10,459
Perhaps you had, miss, but she often talks in this way towards night.

547
00:37:11,400 --> 00:37:13,419
In the morning, she is calmer.

548
00:37:14,339 --> 00:37:15,339
I rose.

549
00:37:15,800 --> 00:37:17,959
Stop, exclaimed Mrs. Reed.

550
00:37:19,019 --> 00:37:20,819
There is another thing I wish to say.

551
00:37:21,639 --> 00:37:22,639
He threatens me.

552
00:37:27,919 --> 00:37:31,506
He sees him laid out with a great wound in his

553
00:37:31,506 --> 00:37:35,881
throat or with a swollen and blackened face.

554
00:37:36,360 --> 00:37:38,580
I am come to a strange pass.

555
00:37:39,500 --> 00:37:40,739
I have heavy troubles.

556
00:37:41,540 --> 00:37:42,639
What is to be done?

557
00:37:43,360 --> 00:37:44,639
How is the money to be had?

558
00:37:45,779 --> 00:37:49,480
Bessie now endeavoured to persuade her to take a sedative draft.

559
00:37:50,660 --> 00:37:52,379
She succeeded with difficulty.

560
00:37:53,639 --> 00:38:00,620
Soon after, Mrs. Reed grew more composed and sank into a dosing state.

561
00:38:01,559 --> 00:38:02,559
I then left her.

562
00:38:04,040 --> 00:38:09,319
More than ten days elapsed before I had again any conversation with her.

563
00:38:10,339 --> 00:38:15,040
She continued either delirious or lethargic, and the doctor forbade

564
00:38:15,040 --> 00:38:17,500
everything which could painfully excite her.

565
00:38:18,400 --> 00:38:22,699
Meantime, I got on as well as I could with Georgiana and Eliza.

566
00:38:23,300 --> 00:38:25,279
They were very cold indeed at first.

567
00:38:26,419 --> 00:38:30,430
Eliza would sit half the day sowing, reading or writing,

568
00:38:30,432 --> 00:38:34,080
and scarcely utter a word either to me or her sister.

569
00:38:35,940 --> 00:38:38,767
Georgiana would chatter nonsense to her canary

570
00:38:38,769 --> 00:38:42,321
bird by the hour and take no notice of me.

571
00:38:43,080 --> 00:38:47,360
But I was determined not to seem at a loss for occupation or amusement.

572
00:38:48,319 --> 00:38:53,000
I had brought my drawing materials with me and they served me for both.

573
00:38:54,860 --> 00:39:00,279
Provided with a case of pencils and some sheets of paper, I used to take a seat

574
00:39:00,281 --> 00:39:06,040
apart from them, near the window, and busy myself in sketching fancy

575
00:39:06,040 --> 00:39:11,760
vignettes, representing any scene that happened momentarily to shape itself in

576
00:39:11,760 --> 00:39:14,360
the ever-shifting kaleidoscope of imagination.

577
00:39:15,480 --> 00:39:21,800
A glimpse of sea between two rocks, the rising moon, and a ship crossing its

578
00:39:21,800 --> 00:39:28,019
disc, a group of reeds and water flags, and a niad's head, crowned with lotus

579
00:39:28,021 --> 00:39:31,875
flowers, rising out of them, an elf sitting in a

580
00:39:31,877 --> 00:39:35,279
hedge sparrow's nest under a wreath of hawthorn bloom.

581
00:39:36,620 --> 00:39:39,480
One morning I fell to sketching a face.

582
00:39:40,400 --> 00:39:44,059
What sort of a face it was to be, I did not care or know.

583
00:39:45,000 --> 00:39:49,339
I took a soft black pencil, gave it a broad point, and worked away.

584
00:39:50,580 --> 00:39:53,997
Soon I had traced on the paper a broad and prominent

585
00:39:53,999 --> 00:39:57,160
forehead and a square lower outline of visage.

586
00:39:57,620 --> 00:39:59,580
That contour gave me pleasure.

587
00:40:00,440 --> 00:40:03,620
My fingers proceeded actively to fill it with features.

588
00:40:04,860 --> 00:40:09,260
Strongly marked horizontal eyebrows must be traced under that brow.

589
00:40:10,400 --> 00:40:16,000
Then followed, naturally, a well-defined nose with a straight ridge and full

590
00:40:16,000 --> 00:40:21,392
nostrils, then a flexible-looking mouth by no means narrow,

591
00:40:21,394 --> 00:40:25,919
then a firm chin with a decided cleft down the middle of it.

592
00:40:26,260 --> 00:40:30,381
Of course, some black whiskers were wanted, and some jetty

593
00:40:30,381 --> 00:40:33,919
hair tuffed it on the temples and waved above the forehead.

594
00:40:35,040 --> 00:40:36,360
Now for the eyes.

595
00:40:37,519 --> 00:40:42,019
I had left them to the last, because they required the most careful working.

596
00:40:42,680 --> 00:40:44,059
I drew them large.

597
00:40:44,680 --> 00:40:45,680
I shaped them well.

598
00:40:46,480 --> 00:40:48,800
The eyelashes I traced long and somber.

599
00:40:49,680 --> 00:40:51,680
The arid's lustrous and large.

600
00:40:53,019 --> 00:40:57,879
Good, but not quite the thing, I thought, as I surveyed the effect.

601
00:40:58,900 --> 00:41:00,559
They want more force and spirit.

602
00:41:01,739 --> 00:41:06,961
And I wrought the shades blacker, that the lights might flash more brilliantly.

603
00:41:07,400 --> 00:41:09,300
A happy touch or two secured success.

604
00:41:09,300 --> 00:41:13,639
Yes, there, I had a friend's face under my gaze.

605
00:41:14,639 --> 00:41:18,139
And what did it signify that those young ladies turned their backs on me?

606
00:41:18,980 --> 00:41:19,980
I looked at it.

607
00:41:20,459 --> 00:41:22,779
I smiled at the speaking likeness.

608
00:41:23,540 --> 00:41:25,400
I was absorbed and content.

609
00:41:27,080 --> 00:41:33,440
Is that a portrait of someone you know, Asterlyzer, who had approached me unnoticed?

610
00:41:33,879 --> 00:41:39,561
I responded that it was merely a fancy head, and hurried it beneath the other sheets.

611
00:41:39,779 --> 00:41:40,839
Of course, I lied.

612
00:41:41,860 --> 00:41:46,540
It was, in fact, a very faithful representation of Mr. Rochester.

613
00:41:47,260 --> 00:41:50,959
But what was that to her, or to anyone but myself?

614
00:41:52,559 --> 00:41:54,580
Georgiana also advanced to look.

615
00:41:55,379 --> 00:41:59,580
The other drawings pleased her much, but she called that an ugly man.

616
00:42:00,680 --> 00:42:02,580
They both seemed surprised at my skill.

617
00:42:03,300 --> 00:42:09,161
I offered to sketch their portraits, and each, in turn, sat for a pencil outline.

618
00:42:09,540 --> 00:42:12,260
Then Georgiana produced her album.

619
00:42:13,160 --> 00:42:15,300
I promised to contribute a watercolor drawing.

620
00:42:16,139 --> 00:42:18,860
This put her at once into good humour.

621
00:42:19,660 --> 00:42:21,080
She proposed a walk in the grounds.

622
00:42:21,860 --> 00:42:26,921
Before we had been out two hours, we were deep in a confidential conversation.

623
00:42:27,980 --> 00:42:31,370
She had favoured me, with a description of the brilliant

624
00:42:31,370 --> 00:42:34,500
winter she had spent in London two seasons ago.

625
00:42:35,620 --> 00:42:40,339
Of the admiration she had there excited, the attention she had received,

626
00:42:41,260 --> 00:42:44,500
and I even got hints of the titled conquest she had made.

627
00:42:45,879 --> 00:42:50,980
In the course of the afternoon and evening, these hints were enlarged on.

628
00:42:52,099 --> 00:42:56,480
Various soft conversations were reported, and sentimental scenes represented.

629
00:42:57,400 --> 00:43:01,353
And, in short, a volume of a novel of fashionable

630
00:43:01,355 --> 00:43:05,019
life was that day improvised by her for my benefit.

631
00:43:06,339 --> 00:43:09,199
The communications were renewed from day to day.

632
00:43:09,860 --> 00:43:14,760
They always ran on the same theme, herself, her loves, and woes.

633
00:43:15,279 --> 00:43:16,500
It was strange.

634
00:43:17,000 --> 00:43:21,660
She never once adverted either to her mother's illness, or her brother's death,

635
00:43:22,319 --> 00:43:25,379
or the present gloomy state of the family prospects.

636
00:43:26,480 --> 00:43:30,968
Her mind seemed wholly taken up with reminiscences of

637
00:43:30,968 --> 00:43:35,180
past gayity, and aspirations after dissipations to come.

638
00:43:36,980 --> 00:43:42,959
She passed about five minutes each day in her mother's sick room, and no more.

639
00:43:44,459 --> 00:43:46,379
Eliza still spoke little.

640
00:43:47,220 --> 00:43:49,620
She had evidently no time to talk.

641
00:43:50,519 --> 00:43:53,677
I never saw a busier person than she seemed to

642
00:43:53,678 --> 00:43:56,860
be, yet it was difficult to say what she did.

643
00:43:57,699 --> 00:44:00,919
Or rather, to discover any result of her diligence.

644
00:44:01,900 --> 00:44:04,040
She had an alarm to call her up early.

645
00:44:04,959 --> 00:44:09,940
I know not how she occupied herself before breakfast, but after that meal,

646
00:44:10,480 --> 00:44:17,061
she divided her time into regular portions, and each hour had its allotted task.

647
00:44:17,440 --> 00:44:22,059
Three times a day she studied a little book, which I found on inspection,

648
00:44:22,559 --> 00:44:24,160
was a common prayer book.

649
00:44:25,400 --> 00:44:29,480
I asked her once what was the great attraction of that volume, and she said,

650
00:44:30,339 --> 00:44:31,339
the rubric.

651
00:44:31,819 --> 00:44:37,279
Three hours she gave to stitching, with gold thread, the border of a square

652
00:44:37,281 --> 00:44:40,440
crimson cloth, almost large enough for a carpet.

653
00:44:41,760 --> 00:44:47,980
In answer to my inquiries after the use of this article, she informed me it was a

654
00:44:47,980 --> 00:44:53,120
covering for the altar of a new church, lately erected near Gateshead.

655
00:44:54,339 --> 00:44:59,279
Two hours she devoted to her diary, two to working by herself in the kitchen

656
00:44:59,281 --> 00:45:03,139
garden, and one to the regulation of her accounts.

657
00:45:04,660 --> 00:45:08,120
She seemed to want no company, no conversation.

658
00:45:09,220 --> 00:45:11,099
I believe she was happy in her way.

659
00:45:11,680 --> 00:45:17,300
This routine sufficed for her, and nothing annoyed her so much as the

660
00:45:17,300 --> 00:45:22,260
occurrence of any incident which forced her to vary its clockwork regularity.

661
00:45:23,379 --> 00:45:28,239
She told me one evening, when more disposed to be communicative than usual,

662
00:45:29,040 --> 00:45:32,483
that John's conduct and the threatened ruin of the

663
00:45:32,483 --> 00:45:36,059
family had been a source of profound affliction to her.

664
00:45:37,000 --> 00:45:43,139
But she had now, she said, settled her mind and formed her resolution.

665
00:45:43,919 --> 00:45:47,239
Her own fortune she had taken care to secure.

666
00:45:48,379 --> 00:45:53,500
And when her mother died, and it was wholly improbable, she tranquilly

667
00:45:53,500 --> 00:45:57,160
remarked, that she should either recover or linger long.

668
00:45:58,220 --> 00:46:03,660
She would execute a long cherished project, seek a retirement where punctual

669
00:46:03,661 --> 00:46:07,824
habits would be permanently secured from disturbance, and

670
00:46:07,826 --> 00:46:12,639
place safe barriers between herself and a frivolous world.

671
00:46:13,739 --> 00:46:16,040
I asked if Georgiana would accompany her.

672
00:46:16,839 --> 00:46:17,839
Of course not.

673
00:46:18,360 --> 00:46:20,580
Georgiana and she had nothing in common.

674
00:46:21,300 --> 00:46:22,319
They never had had.

675
00:46:23,160 --> 00:46:26,779
She would not be burdened with her society for any consideration.

676
00:46:28,019 --> 00:46:34,180
Georgiana should take her own course, and she, Eliza, would take hers.

677
00:46:36,099 --> 00:46:42,000
Georgiana, when not unburdening her heart to me, spent most of her time in lying on

678
00:46:42,000 --> 00:46:47,459
the sofa, fretting about the dullness of the house, and wishing over and over again

679
00:46:47,461 --> 00:46:51,860
that her aunt Gibson would send her an invitation up to town.

680
00:46:53,120 --> 00:46:56,726
It would be so much better, she said, if she could only

681
00:46:56,726 --> 00:47:00,300
get out of the way for a month or two, till all was over.

682
00:47:01,559 --> 00:47:07,900
I did not ask what she meant by all being over, but I suppose she referred to the

683
00:47:07,900 --> 00:47:13,019
expected decease of her mother, and the gloomy sequel of funeral rights.

684
00:47:14,260 --> 00:47:19,480
Eliza generally took no more notice of her sister's indolence and complaints than if

685
00:47:19,480 --> 00:47:23,040
no such murmuring, lounging object had been before her.

686
00:47:23,940 --> 00:47:30,239
One day, however, as she put away her account book, and unfolded her embroidery,

687
00:47:31,059 --> 00:47:32,739
she suddenly took her up thus.

688
00:47:34,919 --> 00:47:39,135
Georgiana, a more vain and absurd animal than you

689
00:47:39,137 --> 00:47:42,480
was certainly never allowed to come by the earth.

690
00:47:43,059 --> 00:47:50,160
You had no right to be born, for you make no use of life, instead of living for in

691
00:47:50,161 --> 00:47:53,620
and with yourself as a reasonable being ought.

692
00:47:54,300 --> 00:47:58,279
You seek only to fasten your feebleness on some other person's strength.

693
00:47:59,019 --> 00:48:03,800
If no one can be found willing to burden her or himself with such a fat,

694
00:48:04,199 --> 00:48:09,959
weak, puffy, useless thing, you cry out that you are ill-treated, neglected,

695
00:48:10,680 --> 00:48:13,040
miserable, then too.

696
00:48:13,779 --> 00:48:18,540
Existence for you must be a scene of continual change and excitement.

697
00:48:19,139 --> 00:48:20,940
Or else the world is a dungeon.

698
00:48:21,819 --> 00:48:27,139
You must be admired, you must be courted, you must be flattered, you must have music

699
00:48:27,141 --> 00:48:31,220
dancing in society, or you languish, you die away.

700
00:48:32,459 --> 00:48:36,038
Have you no sense to devise a system which will make you

701
00:48:36,040 --> 00:48:40,000
independent of all efforts and all wills, but your own?

702
00:48:40,940 --> 00:48:43,699
Take one day, share it into sections.

703
00:48:44,480 --> 00:48:49,360
To each section apportion its task, leave no stray unemployed quarters of an

704
00:48:49,360 --> 00:48:53,779
hour, ten minutes, five minutes, include all.

705
00:48:54,839 --> 00:48:59,940
Do each piece of business in its turn with method, with rigid regularity.

706
00:49:00,680 --> 00:49:06,279
The day will close almost before you are aware it has begun, and you are indebted

707
00:49:06,281 --> 00:49:09,980
to no one for helping you to get rid of one vacant moment.

708
00:49:11,440 --> 00:49:16,900
You have had to seek no one's company, conversation, sympathy, forbearance,

709
00:49:17,440 --> 00:49:21,660
you have lived, in short, as an independent being ought to do.

710
00:49:22,480 --> 00:49:26,451
Take this advice, the first and last I shall offer you,

711
00:49:26,451 --> 00:49:29,800
then you will not want me or anyone else happen what may.

712
00:49:31,500 --> 00:49:32,519
Neglect it.

713
00:49:33,379 --> 00:49:38,180
Go on as here to for craving, whining and idling, and suffer the results of your

714
00:49:38,180 --> 00:49:41,239
idiocy, however bad and insufferable they may be.

715
00:49:42,360 --> 00:49:44,260
I tell you this plainly, and listen.

716
00:49:45,500 --> 00:49:48,341
For though I shall no more repeat what I am

717
00:49:48,343 --> 00:49:52,281
now about to say, I shall steadily act on it.

718
00:49:53,199 --> 00:49:56,480
After my mother's death, I wash my hands of you.

719
00:49:57,599 --> 00:50:02,239
From the day her coffin is carried to the vault in Gateshead Church, you and I will

720
00:50:02,241 --> 00:50:05,160
be as separate as if we had never known each other.

721
00:50:06,080 --> 00:50:10,900
You need not think that because we chance to be born of the same parents,

722
00:50:11,699 --> 00:50:15,879
I shall suffer you to fasten me down by even the feebleest claim.

723
00:50:16,919 --> 00:50:18,040
I can tell you this.

724
00:50:18,959 --> 00:50:24,360
If the whole human race, ourselves accepted, were swept away, and we too

725
00:50:24,360 --> 00:50:27,616
stood alone on the earth, I would leave you in

726
00:50:27,616 --> 00:50:31,141
the old world, and but take myself to the new.

727
00:50:32,519 --> 00:50:33,559
She closed her lips.

728
00:50:35,040 --> 00:50:37,156
You might have spared yourself the trouble

729
00:50:37,158 --> 00:50:40,120
of delivering that tirade, answer Georgiana.

730
00:50:40,779 --> 00:50:46,339
Everybody knows you are the most selfish, heartless creature in existence,

731
00:50:47,239 --> 00:50:49,919
and I know your spiteful hatred towards me.

732
00:50:51,260 --> 00:50:56,421
I have had a specimen of it before, in the trick you played me about Lord Edwin Veer.

733
00:50:57,360 --> 00:51:03,220
You could not bear me to be raised above you, to have a title, to be received into

734
00:51:03,220 --> 00:51:09,720
circles where you dare not show your face, and so you acted the spy and informer,

735
00:51:10,279 --> 00:51:12,800
and ruined my prospects forever.

736
00:51:14,419 --> 00:51:18,900
Georgiana took out her handkerchief and blew her nose for an hour afterwards.

737
00:51:19,860 --> 00:51:24,279
Eliza sat cold, impassable, and assiduously industrious.

738
00:51:25,160 --> 00:51:29,620
True, generous feeling is made small account of by some, but here were two

739
00:51:29,620 --> 00:51:33,332
natures rendered, the one intolerably acrid, the

740
00:51:33,334 --> 00:51:36,580
other despicably saverless for the want of it.

741
00:51:37,319 --> 00:51:43,599
Feeling without judgment is a washy draft indeed, but judgment, untempered by

742
00:51:43,601 --> 00:51:48,019
feeling, is too bitter and husky a morsel for human degradation.

743
00:51:48,021 --> 00:51:52,480
It was a wet and windy afternoon.

744
00:51:53,319 --> 00:51:57,099
Georgiana had fallen asleep on the sofa over the perusal of a novel.

745
00:51:58,059 --> 00:52:02,040
Eliza was gone to attend a saint's day service at the new church.

746
00:52:02,839 --> 00:52:06,559
For in matters of religion, she was a rigid formalist.

747
00:52:07,279 --> 00:52:09,883
No weather ever prevented the punctual discharge of

748
00:52:09,885 --> 00:52:14,440
what she considered her devotional duties, fair or foul.

749
00:52:15,160 --> 00:52:21,461
She went to church thrice every Sunday, and as often on weekdays as there were prayers.

750
00:52:21,959 --> 00:52:25,500
I butthought myself to go upstairs and see how the

751
00:52:25,500 --> 00:52:28,900
dying woman sped, who lay there almost unheeded.

752
00:52:29,660 --> 00:52:33,040
The very servants paid her but a remittant attention.

753
00:52:33,839 --> 00:52:36,273
The hired nurse, being little looked after,

754
00:52:36,273 --> 00:52:39,521
would slip out of the room whenever she could.

755
00:52:39,980 --> 00:52:43,627
Bessie was faithful, but she had her own family to

756
00:52:43,629 --> 00:52:47,000
mind, and could only come occasionally to the hall.

757
00:52:47,419 --> 00:52:50,680
I found the sick room unwatched as I had expected.

758
00:52:51,419 --> 00:52:52,580
No nurse was there.

759
00:52:53,120 --> 00:52:56,860
The patient lay still, and seemingly lethargic.

760
00:52:57,580 --> 00:52:59,919
Her livid face sunk in the pillows.

761
00:53:00,819 --> 00:53:02,339
The fire was dying in the great.

762
00:53:03,180 --> 00:53:08,279
I renewed the fuel, rearranged the bedclothes, gazed a while on her,

763
00:53:08,760 --> 00:53:13,580
who could not now gaze on me, and then I moved away to the window.

764
00:53:14,459 --> 00:53:19,059
The rain beat strongly against the pains, the wind blew tempestuously.

765
00:53:20,440 --> 00:53:25,739
One lies there, I thought, who will soon be beyond the war of earthly elements.

766
00:53:27,000 --> 00:53:31,042
Wither will that spirit, now struggling to quit its

767
00:53:31,042 --> 00:53:34,381
material tenement, flit when it length released.

768
00:53:35,779 --> 00:53:41,580
In pondering the great mystery, I thought of Helen Burns, recalled her

769
00:53:41,580 --> 00:53:47,260
dying words, her faith, her doctrine of the equality of disembodied souls.

770
00:53:48,379 --> 00:53:53,180
I was still listening in thought to her well-remembered tones, still picturing her

771
00:53:53,180 --> 00:53:59,919
pale and spiritual aspect, her wasted face and sublime gaze, as she lay on her placid

772
00:53:59,921 --> 00:54:04,819
deathbed, and whispered her longing to be restored to her divine father's bosom,

773
00:54:05,739 --> 00:54:08,639
when a feeble voice murmured from the couch behind.

774
00:54:09,720 --> 00:54:10,720
Who is that?

775
00:54:12,000 --> 00:54:15,519
I knew Mrs. Reed had not spoken for days, was she reviving?

776
00:54:16,019 --> 00:54:17,019
I went up to her.

777
00:54:17,739 --> 00:54:19,099
It is I, aren't Reed?

778
00:54:20,120 --> 00:54:22,080
Who I was her answer?

779
00:54:23,040 --> 00:54:24,040
Who are you?

780
00:54:24,940 --> 00:54:28,500
Looking at me with surprise and a sort of alarm, but still not wildly.

781
00:54:29,480 --> 00:54:31,900
You are quite a stranger to me, where is Bessie?

782
00:54:33,139 --> 00:54:34,720
She is at the lodge aren't.

783
00:54:35,559 --> 00:54:38,300
Aren't, she repeated, who calls me aunt?

784
00:54:39,139 --> 00:54:42,120
You are not one of the gibson's, and yet I know you.

785
00:54:42,860 --> 00:54:46,540
That face and the eyes and forehead are quiet familiar to me.

786
00:54:47,099 --> 00:54:50,819
You are like, why, you are like Jane Eyre?

787
00:54:51,260 --> 00:54:52,319
I said nothing.

788
00:54:53,040 --> 00:54:55,940
I was afraid of occasioning some shock by declaring my identity.

789
00:54:56,800 --> 00:55:00,080
Yet said she, I am afraid it is a mistake.

790
00:55:00,900 --> 00:55:02,139
My thoughts deceive me.

791
00:55:02,760 --> 00:55:06,847
I wished to see Jane Eyre, and I fancy a likeness when

792
00:55:06,847 --> 00:55:11,160
none exists, besides in eight years she must be so changed.

793
00:55:12,239 --> 00:55:18,459
I now gently assured her that I was the person she supposed and desired me to be,

794
00:55:19,400 --> 00:55:23,900
and seeing that I was understood, and that her senses were quite collected,

795
00:55:24,620 --> 00:55:28,559
I explained how Bessie had sent her husband to fetch me from Thornfield.

796
00:55:29,839 --> 00:55:33,900
I am very ill, I know, she said, air long.

797
00:55:34,559 --> 00:55:39,620
I was trying to turn myself a few minutes since, and find I cannot move a limb.

798
00:55:40,680 --> 00:55:43,660
It is as well I should ease my mind before I die.

799
00:55:45,099 --> 00:55:51,601
What we think little of in health burdens us at such an hour as the present is to me.

800
00:55:53,519 --> 00:55:55,319
Is the no one in the room but you?

801
00:55:56,199 --> 00:55:58,120
I assured her we were alone.

802
00:55:59,239 --> 00:56:02,860
Well, I have twice done you are wrong, which I regret now.

803
00:56:04,040 --> 00:56:06,171
One was in breaking the promise which I gave

804
00:56:06,173 --> 00:56:09,400
my husband to bring you up as my own child.

805
00:56:09,620 --> 00:56:11,300
The other, she stopped.

806
00:56:12,559 --> 00:56:18,160
After all, it is of no great importance, perhaps, she murmured to herself,

807
00:56:18,599 --> 00:56:21,019
and then I may get better.

808
00:56:21,940 --> 00:56:24,099
And to humble myself so to her is painful.

809
00:56:25,080 --> 00:56:27,720
She made an effort to alter her position, but failed.

810
00:56:28,540 --> 00:56:29,559
Her face changed.

811
00:56:30,220 --> 00:56:34,599
She seemed to experience some inward sensation, the precursor perhaps,

812
00:56:34,980 --> 00:56:36,300
of the last pang.

813
00:56:37,500 --> 00:56:38,919
Well, I must get it over.

814
00:56:39,540 --> 00:56:40,800
Eternity is before me.

815
00:56:41,059 --> 00:56:42,120
I had better tell her.

816
00:56:43,199 --> 00:56:47,239
Go to my dressing-case, open it, and take out a letter you will see there.

817
00:56:48,160 --> 00:56:49,339
I obeyed her directions.

818
00:56:50,639 --> 00:56:52,220
Read the letter, she said.

819
00:56:53,019 --> 00:56:54,819
It was short and thus conceived.

820
00:56:56,019 --> 00:57:02,459
Madam, will you have the goodness to send me the address of my niece, Jane Eyre,

821
00:57:03,019 --> 00:57:04,419
and to tell me how she is?

822
00:57:05,739 --> 00:57:10,559
It is my intention to write shortly, and desire her to come to me at Madera.

823
00:57:11,400 --> 00:57:14,980
Providence has blessed my endeavors to secure a competency.

824
00:57:15,919 --> 00:57:19,839
And as I am unmarried and childless, I wish to adopt her during my life,

825
00:57:20,319 --> 00:57:23,199
and bequeath her at my death whatever I may have to leave.

826
00:57:24,239 --> 00:57:27,379
I am madam, etc., etc.

827
00:57:27,959 --> 00:57:29,680
John Eyre, Madera.

828
00:57:30,319 --> 00:57:32,099
It was dated three years back.

829
00:57:33,360 --> 00:57:34,779
Why did I never hear of this?

830
00:57:35,819 --> 00:57:36,819
I asked.

831
00:57:37,500 --> 00:57:41,644
Because I disliked you too fixidly and thoroughly,

832
00:57:41,644 --> 00:57:44,980
ever to lend a hand in lifting you to prosperity.

833
00:57:46,180 --> 00:57:51,300
I could not forget your conduct to me, Jane, the fury with which you once turned

834
00:57:51,300 --> 00:57:56,580
on me, the tone in which you declared you abhorred me, the worst of anybody in the

835
00:57:56,580 --> 00:58:02,440
world, the unchilded-like look and voice with which you affirmed that the very

836
00:58:02,440 --> 00:58:05,807
thought of me made you sick, and asserted

837
00:58:05,807 --> 00:58:10,061
that I had treated you with miserable cruelty.

838
00:58:11,220 --> 00:58:13,559
I could not forget my own sensations.

839
00:58:14,440 --> 00:58:20,500
When you thus started up and poured out the venom of your mind, I felt fear,

840
00:58:21,120 --> 00:58:24,275
as if an animal that I had struck or pushed had looked

841
00:58:24,277 --> 00:58:27,319
up at me with human eyes and cursed me in a man's voice.

842
00:58:28,339 --> 00:58:31,639
Bring me some water, oh make haste.

843
00:58:31,641 --> 00:58:36,620
Dear Mrs. Reid said I, as I offered her the draft she required.

844
00:58:37,620 --> 00:58:39,120
Think no more of all this.

845
00:58:40,220 --> 00:58:41,940
Let it pass away from your mind.

846
00:58:42,720 --> 00:58:44,400
Forgive me for my passionate language.

847
00:58:45,019 --> 00:58:49,419
I was a child then, eight, nine years of past since that day.

848
00:58:50,239 --> 00:58:53,459
She he did nothing of what I said, but when she had

849
00:58:53,461 --> 00:58:57,339
tasted the water and drawn breath, she went on thus.

850
00:58:58,760 --> 00:59:03,440
I tell you, I could not forget it, and I took my revenge.

851
00:59:04,300 --> 00:59:07,375
For you to be adopted by your uncle and placed in a

852
00:59:07,375 --> 00:59:10,879
state of ease and comfort was what I could not endure.

853
00:59:11,300 --> 00:59:12,300
I wrote to him.

854
00:59:12,750 --> 00:59:16,959
I said I was sorry for his disappointment, but Jane Eyre was dead.

855
00:59:17,739 --> 00:59:20,379
She had died of typhus fever at lowered.

856
00:59:21,639 --> 00:59:22,900
Now act as you please.

857
00:59:23,620 --> 00:59:25,480
Write and contradict my assertion.

858
00:59:26,040 --> 00:59:28,339
Expose my falsehood as soon as you like.

859
00:59:29,099 --> 00:59:31,199
You were born, I think, to be my torment.

860
00:59:32,300 --> 00:59:36,824
My last hour is racked by the recollection of a deed which,

861
00:59:36,826 --> 00:59:39,720
but for you, I should never have been tempted to commit.

862
00:59:41,120 --> 00:59:46,220
If you could but be persuaded to think no more of it aren't, and to regard me with

863
00:59:46,220 --> 00:59:51,059
kindness and forgiveness, you have a very bad disposition.

864
00:59:52,040 --> 00:59:56,900
Said she, and one to this day, I feel it impossible to understand,

865
00:59:57,540 --> 01:00:02,540
how for nine years you could be patient and quiescent under any treatment,

866
01:00:03,180 --> 01:00:08,639
and in the tenth breakout all fire and violence I can never comprehend.

867
01:00:10,059 --> 01:00:13,860
My disposition is not so bad as you think.

868
01:00:14,739 --> 01:00:18,059
I am passionate, but not vindictive.

869
01:00:19,139 --> 01:00:24,319
Many a time as a little child, I should have been glad to love you if you

870
01:00:24,321 --> 01:00:28,660
would have let me, and I long earnestly to be reconciled to you now.

871
01:00:29,279 --> 01:00:34,099
Kiss me aunt, I approached my cheek to her lips, she would not touch it.

872
01:00:35,160 --> 01:00:40,739
She said I oppressed her by leaning over the bed, and again demanded water.

873
01:00:41,760 --> 01:00:46,940
As I laid her down, for I raised her and supported her on my arm while she drank.

874
01:00:47,879 --> 01:00:50,620
I covered her ice cold and clammy hand with mine.

875
01:00:51,519 --> 01:00:55,440
The feeble fingers shrank from my touch, the glazing eyes shunned my gaze.

876
01:00:56,639 --> 01:01:02,220
Love me then, or hate me as you will, I said at last, you have my full and free

877
01:01:02,220 --> 01:01:05,620
forgiveness, ask now for gods and be at peace.

878
01:01:07,459 --> 01:01:08,919
Poor suffering woman.

879
01:01:09,760 --> 01:01:13,559
It was too late for her to make now the effort to change her habitual frame of

880
01:01:13,561 --> 01:01:19,180
mind, living she had ever hated me, dying she must hate me still.

881
01:01:20,339 --> 01:01:22,760
The nurse now entered, and Bessie followed.

882
01:01:23,819 --> 01:01:28,239
I yet lingered half an hour longer, hoping to see some sign of amity,

883
01:01:28,400 --> 01:01:29,459
but she gave none.

884
01:01:30,360 --> 01:01:34,440
She was fast relapsing into stupor, nor did her mind again rally.

885
01:01:35,459 --> 01:01:37,860
At 12 o'clock that night, she died.

886
01:01:39,680 --> 01:01:44,139
I was not present to close her eyes, nor were either of her daughters.

887
01:01:45,199 --> 01:01:48,199
They came to tell us the next morning that all was over.

888
01:01:49,160 --> 01:01:51,279
She was by that time laid out.

889
01:01:52,339 --> 01:01:54,019
Eliza and I went to look at her.

890
01:01:54,779 --> 01:01:59,980
Georgiana, who had burst out into loud weeping, said she dared not go.

891
01:02:01,120 --> 01:02:06,180
There was stretched Sarah Reed's once robust and active frame, rigid and still.

892
01:02:07,000 --> 01:02:09,800
Her eye of flint was covered with its cold lid.

893
01:02:10,580 --> 01:02:15,480
Her brow and strong traits wore yet the impress of her inexorable soul.

894
01:02:16,919 --> 01:02:20,279
A strange and solemn object was that corpse to me.

895
01:02:21,620 --> 01:02:27,180
I gazed on it with gloom and pain, nothing soft, nothing sweet, nothing

896
01:02:27,180 --> 01:02:30,540
pitying or hopeful, or subduing did it inspire.

897
01:02:31,639 --> 01:02:37,819
Only a great in anguish for her woes, not my loss, and a somber tearless dismay

898
01:02:37,821 --> 01:02:40,839
at the fearfulness of death in such a form.

899
01:02:42,639 --> 01:02:48,519
Eliza surveyed her parent calmly after a silence of some minutes she observed.

900
01:02:49,260 --> 01:02:53,071
With her constitution, she should have lived to a

901
01:02:53,072 --> 01:02:56,040
good old age, her life was shortened by trouble.

902
01:02:56,919 --> 01:03:01,370
And then a spasm constricted her mouth for an instant as

903
01:03:01,372 --> 01:03:05,099
it passed away she turned and left the room and so did I.

904
01:03:06,199 --> 01:03:07,819
Neither of us had dropped a tear.
